The reason given at the bottom of the page for the fi'uvla is for
five-letter rafsi can be formed. I can see how this has some advantages for
structured usage, and really no better application of this lojban feature
than names used in international discourse. Perhaps its still ideal to add
another column for a cmene version, or just make the 'lojban approximation'
into a 'recommended cmene' column?

